WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.554
Here is where the data model pays off.

2
00:00:03.554 --> 00:00:08.374
In this lesson, you will learn to filter shipment amounts by a product name

3
00:00:08.374 --> 00:00:13.193
that lives in a different table, and see how the relationship makes it work.

4
00:00:13.193 --> 00:00:15.603
Then we start our first calculated column.

5
00:00:15.603 --> 00:00:16.980
Let's connect the dots!

6
00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:21.902
We continue our measure with a third filter.

7
00:00:21.902 --> 00:00:28.280
After the order status filter, I add FILTER on the Product table, where Product equals Milk Bars.

8
00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:32.783
Notice:

9
00:00:32.783 --> 00:00:35.082
Shipments and Product are different tables.

10
00:00:35.082 --> 00:00:39.680
This works because they are connected by a relationship in the model.

11
00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:45.538
I add the measure to a card. The answer:

12
00:00:45.538 --> 00:00:48.327
one hundred thirty six point nine nine thousand.

13
00:00:48.327 --> 00:00:52.860
That is the delivered amount of Milk Bars for S P zero one.

14
00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:00.419
I add a clear title:

15
00:01:00.419 --> 00:01:05.265
SP01 Shipment Amount that are delivered and related to only Milk Bars.

16
00:01:05.265 --> 00:01:06.880
Long, but very clear!

17
00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:45.985
Now the page tells a story:

18
00:01:45.985 --> 00:01:50.725
overall amount, then one salesperson, then delivered only, then one product.

19
00:01:50.725 --> 00:01:52.880
Each filter narrows the answer.

20
00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:06.089
Next, a different tool: a calculated column.

21
00:02:06.089 --> 00:02:10.700
I open the Shipments table in Table view and click New column.

22
00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:56.539
The new column is called Total Amount:

23
00:02:56.539 --> 00:02:58.781
Shipments, Amount, times Shipments, Boxes.

24
00:02:58.781 --> 00:03:01.920
It is calculated once for every row.

25
00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:11.093
Now each row has its own total.

26
00:03:11.093 --> 00:03:13.787
Measures summarize, columns calculate row by row.

27
00:03:13.787 --> 00:03:16.480
We compare them in the next lesson!

